            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. When an employee with one (1) year or more of Bargaining Unit seniority transfers out of the Bargaining Unit, the employee shall retain but not accumulate the Bargaining Unit seniority held at the time of transfer. An employee who transfers out of the Bargaining Unit shall only retain the Bargaining Unit seniority for a period not to exceed twelve (12) months from the date of transfer. Such employee may only displace back into the Bargaining Unit within this same 12 month period. In the event the employee transfers or displaces back into the Bargaining Unit the employee shall apply their retained seniority in accordance with the terms of this Article.",
            "block_bbox": [
                98,
                103,
                723,
                325
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 0,
